Original commit body from 3e156ecaac78b5230bbcd377ad4bf591aed7373b:

py.py walked function bodies and module code, and for a ClassDef only its
decorators, so a statement in the class body itself -- field =
models.CharField(...), requests.get(...) -- emitted no calls edge and no
module_attr_ref (INV-foluz). verify-claims read a class-body secret ->
network flow as confirmed with no evidence.

The class body's own statements (defs and nested classes excluded) are now
walked like module code under the innermost class, looked up by AST node
id (class_symbol_by_node_id, threaded through FileAnalysis) so Django's
many same-named Meta classes do not collide. The scope is the enclosing
function's LEGB chain, if any, plus a frame for the class body's bindings.

